  "notes": "10-segment, 6-point lathe: 80 triangles, one closed shell, three materials.  The profile is asymmetric in length: full width by 12% of the length, widest at 42%, then a 58%-long taper to the point.  Groove = the two vertex columns at 72/108 degrees pulled in 24%, not a cut; the column at 0-36 degrees is lifted 14% into a narrow pale starchy crest (paper slot).  The blunt pole is pushed 7.5% of the body length into the kernel, so the end fan becomes a concave germ dimple painted wood_dark, and a 180-degree turn about Y puts that germ and the crest on the side the shared camera sees.  The underside column is raised to 80% of the radius for a small resting flat.  fit_bounds pins 0.020/0.013/0.012 m, so finish() does not rescale.",
